Package: gpim
Type: Package
Title: Probabilistic index models for hierarchical survival outcomes
Version: 0.0.1
Authors@R: c(person("Xi", "Fang", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "xfang@mcw.edu"),
    person("Zhiqiang", "Cao", role = "aut"),
    person("Lu", "Mao", role = "aut"),
    person("Fan", "Li", role = "aut"))
Description: Fits probabilistic index regression models for prioritized
    composite survival outcomes from long-format event records. Complete-history,
    Horvitz-Thompson, and determinant-level censoring adjustments are available
    with identity, logit, and probit links. Cox and Breslow censoring
    estimation, martingale-adjusted sandwich inference, formula interfaces,
    coefficient trajectories, and convergence diagnostics are included.
    The methods are described in Fang, Cao, Mao, and Li (2026),
    "Probabilistic index models for hierarchical survival outcomes"
    (manuscript under review).
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
